"""HXC 100-Cycle Novelty-Audited Structure + Theorem Inventor — one-cell Colab runner.

Paste this entire script into one Google Colab cell, or upload it and run:

    %run /content/HXC_100_CYCLE_NOVELTY_AUDITED_MATH_INVENTOR_COLAB_V10.py

This system runs the complete HXC discovery pipeline repeatedly. Each cycle
constructs a non-degenerate finite operation, rejects known catalogues and
earlier cycle discoveries, synthesises a non-seeded identity, finds an
independent countermodel, assigns fresh Unicode glyphs, emits Lean 4 proofs,
and optionally verifies the cycle with the Lean kernel.

Novelty is audited in layers:
  * isomorphism and anti-isomorphism deduplication;
  * complete generated small-order algebra-family catalogues;
  * category-resolved comparison-bank countermodels;
  * exhaustive order-2 and order-3 countermodels satisfying every advertised
    positive law, establishing finite semantic independence;
  * exact identity matching against downloaded public equation databases;
  * Lean kernel verification of the structure, theorem, catalogue
    countermodel, and positive-law independence witness.

Historical novelty is never asserted automatically. The output distinguishes
verified finite novelty, database non-match, database scope, and unverified
literature novelty.
"""

